When a pull fails, the program prints git's message, with the directory added to the "error:"
prefix so that the reader knows which clone failed.

The program also tries to delete the two lines "Please, commit your changes or stash them before
you can merge." and "Aborting", but git has not used that wording for years (it now says "Please
commit your changes or stash them before you merge."), so those lines are not deleted.  The goal
file records the current behavior.
